       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. At twice the maximum, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is substantial, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**: 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses**: for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another regimen**: tell me the intended dose and frequency.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
